      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Build a low-risk movement-level BFS variant. Preserve the full key (exact player cell plus canonical sorted boxes) and current discovery/tie semantics. Target per-successor linear box scans, push-time bubble sorting, repeated hashing, record alignment, and allocation/queue locality; use collision-checked hashes and no fixed input limits. Audit the existing R/L/U/D plus LIFO ordering before any queue change, since output must remain shortest and direction-tie correct. Do not alter infrastructure or hard-code inputs.\",\"B\":\"Research an independent exact push-macro solver. A macro edge must charge every walking step and push, reconstruct the full move string, and retain the required shortest lexicographic result. Player-reachability compression is unsafe if it merges paths without distance and lexicographic tie handling; use a rigorously tie-aware Dijkstra-style design or reject it. Return a candidate only if it is demonstrably equivalent and faster than movement BFS.\",\"C\":\"Research safe state-space pruning while retaining the baseline search semantics. Improve static reverse-push analysis to goal-specific reachability and, where worthwhile, use cached box-to-goal matching infeasibility; only add deadlock rules with a proof of safety (for example, fully blocked 2x2 cases). Keep preprocessing/filter overhead gated because the measured run is short, and never prune from an unproven heuristic. Preserve literal board spaces and general valid board sizes.\",\"G\":\"Treat A, B, and C as competing alternatives, not additive gains. Validate exact output semantics and prescribed correctness before integration; combine A and C only if state ordering and keys remain compatible, and evaluate B as a replacement engine. Accept only a material repeated win over the 4.939–5.103 ms baseline spread, retaining the fastest valid program. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or input-specific behavior.\",\"analysis\":\"The valid baseline averages 5.010 ms over three samples and only four correctness cases, so startup, allocation, and measurement noise matter; heavyweight preprocessing and parallel frontier work on the 4-core ARM64 target are low priority. The source performs BFS one player move at a time, with costly box scans, push sorting, hashing, and table/pool traffic. Its head-insert frontier makes traversal order non-obvious, so preserving shortest-path tie behavior is as important as reducing search work.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"d07e12f5cf7aea9ac7b0ef15829398c352dac9a89566ef58a10b82473da66bda\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Build a low-risk movement-level BFS variant. Preserve the full key (exact player cell plus canonical sorted boxes) and current discovery/tie semantics. Target per-successor linear box scans, push-time bubble sorting, repeated hashing, record alignment, and allocation/queue locality; use collision-checked hashes and no fixed input limits. Audit the existing R/L/U/D plus LIFO ordering before any queue change, since output must remain shortest and direction-tie correct. Do not alter infrastructure or hard-code inputs.\",\"B\":\"Research an independent exact push-macro solver. A macro edge must charge every walking step and push, reconstruct the full move string, and retain the required shortest lexicographic result. Player-reachability compression is unsafe if it merges paths without distance and lexicographic tie handling; use a rigorously tie-aware Dijkstra-style design or reject it. Return a candidate only if it is demonstrably equivalent and faster than movement BFS.\",\"C\":\"Research safe state-space pruning while retaining the baseline search semantics. Improve static reverse-push analysis to goal-specific reachability and, where worthwhile, use cached box-to-goal matching infeasibility; only add deadlock rules with a proof of safety (for example, fully blocked 2x2 cases). Keep preprocessing/filter overhead gated because the measured run is short, and never prune from an unproven heuristic. Preserve literal board spaces and general valid board sizes.\",\"G\":\"Treat A, B, and C as competing alternatives, not additive gains. Validate exact output semantics and prescribed correctness before integration; combine A and C only if state ordering and keys remain compatible, and evaluate B as a replacement engine. Accept only a material repeated win over the 4.939–5.103 ms baseline spread, retaining the fastest valid program. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or input-specific behavior.\",\"analysis\":\"The valid baseline averages 5.010 ms over three samples and only four correctness cases, so startup, allocation, and measurement noise matter; heavyweight preprocessing and parallel frontier work on the 4-core ARM64 target are low priority. The source performs BFS one player move at a time, with costly box scans, push sorting, hashing, and table/pool traffic. Its head-insert frontier makes traversal order non-obvious, so preserving shortest-path tie behavior is as important as reducing search work.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"be4c692e31f44356b933f722b3a283cc\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"d07e12f5cf7aea9ac7b0ef15829398c352dac9a89566ef58a10b82473da66bda\",\"session_id\":\"15219a6fd62b4dcb91b395dcd4ae03d5\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"1c3c027a3869ec5cdd65c05a89169b67eb4fc6f2e6b1fd2cb4fcd1d228fb7ded\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":13182,\"output_tokens\":11889,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":11394}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":25071,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
